    "verdict_reason": "T(beta) is significantly non-flat (best=boltzmann, beats flat by Delta-AIC=16.7), but the Wang-He form is not the AIC-minimum. Temperature dependence is real; functional-form identification is ambiguous at L=10.",
    "CORRECTED_INTERPRETATION_2026_05_29": "The raw verdict above OVERSTATES the result and must NOT be cited at face value. Honest reading after scrutiny: the transport TIME T(beta) is effectively FLAT. It varies only 1.4% across the entire physical thermal regime (beta=200 down to beta=1, over which the state goes from pure ground state to gs_pop=0.169). The full 3.3% 'total variation' is produced almost entirely by the single hottest point (beta=0.5), where the state is near-maximally mixed (N_eff=129) and the dip/reappear extraction is least reliable. The AIC 'preference' for Boltzmann is fitting a near-zero coefficient (a=-0.016, i.e. essentially the flat value with a microscopic correction); the Wang-He fit outright FAILED (R2=-0.67, covariance not estimable, params -> 1e-11). CONCLUSION: the transport-TIME channel does NOT carry the horizon signal at N=10. This DISSOCIATES from the transport-AMPLITUDE channel (SIM-027/028), which degraded 95% and beat the washout null control on the SAME TFD states. The functional-form / BTZ-curve claim is NOT supportable from the transport time at workstation-accessible sizes; do not put it in a paper. SCRIPT BUG: the verdict logic gates on Delta-AIC>4 over flat WITHOUT a magnitude floor, so it crowns a model on a sub-1.5% wiggle. A corrected gate must also require the fitted shape variation to exceed a physical threshold (e.g. >10% of T_cold) AND the chosen model's params to be non-degenerate.",
